   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 1. Physics-Informed Neural Networks (PINNs)\n",
    "\n",
    "**The Vision:**\n",
    "Embed Maxwell's equations directly into neural network architectures, creating models that are guaranteed to satisfy physical laws while learning from data.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Key Advantages:**\n",
    "- **Physics by construction**: Models automatically satisfy conservation laws\n",
    "- **Data efficiency**: Orders of magnitude less training data required\n",
    "- **Improved generalization**: Physical principles don't change with parameter ranges\n",
    "- **Interpretability**: Failures traceable to specific physics violations\n",
    "\n",
    "**Research Challenges:**\n",
    "- **Multi-physics integration**: Combining electromagnetic, thermal, and structural physics\n",
    "- **Boundary condition enforcement**: Automatic handling of complex geometries\n",
    "- **Loss function balancing**: Optimizing weights for competing physics constraints\n",
    "- **Computational efficiency**: Automatic differentiation overhead\n",
    "\n",
    "**Expected Timeline:** 2-5 years for practical implementation"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
    "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Physics-Informed Neural Networks Concept\n",
    "def demonstrate_pinn_concept():\n",
    "    \"\"\"Illustrate the PINN concept for electromagnetic design\"\"\"\n",
    "    \n",
    "    print(\"=== PHYSICS-INFORMED NEURAL NETWORKS CONCEPT ===\")\n",
    "    print()\n",
    "    \n",
    "    print(\"🔬 TRADITIONAL NEURAL NETWORK:\")\n",
    "    print(\"   Loss = MSE(Predicted, Actual)\")\n",
    "    print(\"   - Learns purely from data\")\n",
    "    print(\"   - May violate physical laws\")\n",
    "    print(\"   - Requires lots of training data\")\n",
    "    print(\"   - Poor extrapolation\")\n",
    "    print()\n",
    "    \n",
    "    print(\"⚛️  PHYSICS-INFORMED NEURAL NETWORK:\")\n",
    "    print(\"   Loss = α×MSE + β×Physics_Loss\")\n",
    "    print(\"   Physics_Loss = ‖∇×E - ∂B/∂t‖² + ‖∇×H + ∂D/∂t‖² + ‖∇·B‖² + ‖∇·D‖²\")\n",
    "    print(\"   - Combines data with physics\")\n",
    "    print(\"   - Satisfies Maxwell's equations\")\n",
    "    print(\"   - Requires much less data\")\n",
    "    print(\"   - Better generalization\")\n",
    "    print()\n",
    "    \n",
    "    print(\"🎯 APPLICATIONS IN ELECTROMAGNETIC DESIGN:\")\n",
    "    applications = [\n",
